:: Fishing Combat Forest Lake
<<effects>>
<<run fishingCombatEffects()>>
<<run fishingAttentionCheck()>>

/* Fishing gets interrupted by an attack */
<<if _fishingDangerEventTriggered>>
	<<fishCombatForestLakeAttackInterrupt $fishing.lake.event>>

/* Player orgasm */
<<elseif $arousal gte $arousalmax>>
	<<fishCombatForestLakeOrgasm>>

/* You've caught the fish */
<<elseif $fishing.combat.fishDistance lte 0>>
	<<fishCombatForestLakeCaught>>

/* Your line has snapped */
<<elseif $fishing.combat.lineHealth lte 0>>
	<<fishCombatForestLakeLineSnapped>>

/* Still fishing */
<<else>>
	<<fishCombatForestLakeMain>>
<</if>>


:: Fishing Forest Lake Cut Line
<<run endFishingCombat()>>
You release the tension on the rod, letting the line go slack. The <<print $fishingHookedFish.type>> pulls harder, and with a sudden snap, the line breaks free. Through the ripples, you catch a glimpse of it darting deeper, finally free.
<br><br>

<<link [[Re-hook the line and cast back out (0:03)|Fishing Forest Lake Wait]]>><<pass 3>><</link>>
<br>
<<link [[Leave|Lake Fishing Rock]]>><</link>>


:: Widgets Fishing Combat Forest Lake [widget]
<<widget "fishCombatForestLakeAttackInterrupt">>
	<<set $fishing.lake.event to "none">>
	<<set $fishing.lake.eventDanger to 0>>
	<<if _args[0] is "wolf">>
		<<include "Fishing Forest Lake Wolf Interrupt Attack">>
	<<elseif _args[0] is "bear">>
		<<include "Fishing Forest Lake Bear Interrupt Attack">>
	<<elseif _args[0] is "boar">>
		<<include "Fishing Forest Lake Boar Interrupt Attack">>
	<<elseif _args[0] is "plant">>
		<<include "Fishing Forest Lake Plant Interrupt Attack">>
	<<else>>
		<<run console.error("fishCombatForestLakeAttackInterrupt: unknown event value: " + _args[0])>>
	<</if>>
<</widget>>


<<widget "fishCombatForestLakeMain">>
	<<run fishCombatAction()>>
	<<fishCombatActionDescription>>
	<<printFishInfo>>
	<br><br>

	<<fishCombatActions "Forest Lake">>
	<<fishingForestLakeCombatDebugLinks>>
<</widget>>

<<widget "fishCombatForestLakeCaught">>
	<<run updateFishRecord($fishingHookedFish.type, $fishingHookedFish.size, "forestLake")>>
	<<run endFishingCombat()>>
	<<run holdCaughtFish($fishingHookedFish.type)>>
	<<set _canEatFish to canEatFishTf($fishingHookedFish)>>

	<<fishingCatchFishText "forestLake">>
	<br><br>

	<<if _canEatFish>>
		It's such a small fish, you could probably fit the whole thing in your mouth.
		<br><br>
	<</if>>

	<<link [[Stow it away|Fishing Forest Lake Keep]]>><</link>>
	<br>
	<<link [["Throw the " + $fishingHookedFish.type + " back"|Fishing Forest Lake Throw Back]]>><</link>>
	<<if _canEatFish>>
		<br>
		<<link [[Eat the fish|Fishing Forest Lake Cat Eat]]>><</link>>
	<</if>>
<</widget>>

<<widget "fishCombatForestLakeLineSnapped">>
	Your line suddenly goes slack, and the <<print $fishingHookedFish.type>> disappears into the depths.
	<<run endFishingCombat()>>
	<br><br>

	<<link [[Re-hook the line and cast back out (0:03)|Fishing Forest Lake Wait]]>><<pass 3>><</link>>
	<br>
	<<link [[Leave|Lake Fishing Rock]]>><</link>>
<</widget>>

<<widget "fishCombatForestLakeOrgasm">>
	<<orgasmFishing "forestLake">>
	The rod slips. By the time you recover yourself, the line has gone slack and the <<print $fishingHookedFish.type>> is gone.
	<<run endFishingCombat()>>
	<br>
	<<link [[Next|Fishing Forest Lake Wait]]>><</link>>
<</widget>>
